1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
[narrator] After challenging Meruem
to a contest in order to buy time,

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Pouf was outside the palace
scattering scales

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
[Shaiapouf] I must hurry, or Lord Meruem
will remember what he should not.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[man 1] We haven't moved forward at all.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
What the hell is the matter?
What's going on up there?

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
[man 2] Shh! Keep quiet, all right?

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[man 3] I heard all senior officers
have collapsed, one after another…

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
like puppets whose strings
have been cut.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[Shaiapouf] After giving the King
6/7 of my body,

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
I'm significantly weaker.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
I've lost so much power.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The scales aren't scattering as well
as I would like.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
And I don't see
any of Pitou's puppets around anywhere.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Does that mean the battle
with the boy is so intense,

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
that aura cannot be spared on puppets?

16
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Even so, I need to hurry
and kill the woman

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
while there's still time.

18
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
[opening theme music playing]

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
[singer singing in English]

20
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
[singer singing in English]

22
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

23
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
DEADLINE X TO X LIVE

24
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Are you telling me that
they didn't run away?

25
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Yeah.

26
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
And you better tie up their hands
and blindfold them.

27
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
I can't let them see me.
No time to explain.

28
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
I understand. That makes sense.

29
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
By the way, why did you bring him along?

30
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Welfin] Hmm? Huh?

31
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
that the woman's
in the underground warehouse.

32
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Let them know that
we're looking to negotiate a deal.

33
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Do that and you're free.

34
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
The fact that I'm doing
the enemy's bidding at all

35
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
may be enough to anger the King.

36
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I'm not about to dig my own grave.

37
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
[Welfin] A lot better than you.

38
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[Palm] It's absolutely critical
that he carries out his mission.

39
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Welfin, once this is all over,
you're free.

40
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
[Welfin] Huh?

41
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Ikalgo] Then go find Gyro.

42
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Huh?

43
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
What do you know?
Just who do you think you are, huh?

44
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
I know that,

45
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
[Welfin] How…

46
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
How did you know about…

47
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
my old name?

48
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
I never told anyone.

49
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
we were friends.

50
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
We were friends?

51
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[Ikalgo] From before.

52
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
[Welfin] Yeah.

53
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[Ikalgo] The Ants are our enemies.

54
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Enemies of the NGL.

55
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Take him with you.

56
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[snarls]

57
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
how do you know?

58
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Wait. What do you mean?

59
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
You just said you wanted me to find Gyro.

60
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
But I…

61
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
I don't know if he's alive.

62
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
I just know he has to be.

63
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Huh?

64
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[Ikalgo] We survived, didn't we?

65
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
So I know. He wouldn't let himself
get digested.

66
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[snarls]

67
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[engine starts]

68
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[door buzzes]

69
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
[Welfin] Damn it.

70
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Damn it!

71
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[groans]

72
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] I really hope you're sure
about this, Pouf.

73
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
It's already been ten minutes,

74
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
and I don't see any sign
of Pitou returning.

75
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[gasps]

76
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
[Welfin] Get out.

77
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Untie yourselves and use
the truck to escape.

78
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Once you're outside,

79
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
you'll realize what's going on.

80
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
[engine starts]

81
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
[beeps]

82
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
[door buzzes]

83
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Stop!

84
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
-[tires screeching]
-Huh?

85
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Wait. Sir Youpi?

86
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
[ominous music playing]

87
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Sir Youpi.

88
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Please, I need to get a message
to the King immediately.

89
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Hmm?

90
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[Menthuthuyoupi]
The underground warehouse?

91
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[Welfin] Right.

92
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
They want to make a trade,
that woman for all their captured allies?

93
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Is that what you're telling me?

94
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
That's right.

95
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Go and tell the King at once.
He's gonna wanna know about it.

96
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
We're having a contest,

97
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
so I don't really need to tell the King.

98
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
If this is the kind of thing
Pouf was expecting,

99
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
well, he's even smarter than I thought.

100
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[coughs]

101
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
All right. You can go.

102
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Sir!

103
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
[Welfin] Chimera Ants are the enemy.

104
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
-Sir Youpi!
-Hmm?

105
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
[Welfin] I have a question for you, sir!

106
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] What is it?

107
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Do you have any memories
from your former life?

108
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Old memories, like before you changed.

109
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Huh?

110
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
You're kidding. Of course not!

111
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
I'm Youpi, the Royal Guard!

112
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
And that's all I've ever been!

113
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Don't ask me stupid questions!

114
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
What? I told you don't… Huh?

115
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Hmm?

116
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
If you try to attack me, I'll fight back.

117
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[grunts]

118
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
you stupid punk!

119
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Yes.

120
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
even one single time.

121
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[dramatic music playing]

122
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
-[high-pitched whine]
-[grunts]

123
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[imperceptible]

124
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
[Shaiapouf sighs] That took much longer
than I expected.

125
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Where's Youpi?

126
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Youpi.

127
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:08,000
No. It can't be.

128
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
All right. We're okay now.

129
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,000
[Ikalgo] What do you mean?

130
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Palm?

131
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[Meruem] In that case,

132
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
I suppose it's all right for me to begin.

133
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
It's too dangerous!

134
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
-The game is--
-[Meruem] The game is off?

135
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[gasps]

136
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Then that means I have won.

137
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
You will tell me everything you know.

138
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[whimpers]

139
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
As we know…

140
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Pitou tried to save and protect her.

141
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:45,000
But Pouf, on the other hand,
tried to kill her.

142
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
To put it in another way,

143
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,000
she's a double-edged sword for the King.

144
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Is it? All right.

145
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
But what about us?
How do you explain our situation?

146
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Wouldn't you say that it's impossible

147
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
for Soldier Ants to side with humans?

148
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
They aren't mutually exclusive after all.

149
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Both of these reactions make sense.

150
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
I guess. I'll concede that point for now.

151
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
But you said that we're okay,
so how do you know that?

152
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[Palm] Twenty minutes have passed
since the initial wave of En

153
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
That's why I think we're okay.

154
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Hmm.

155
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Yeah, I still don't get it.
What the hell is going on here, Palm?

156
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
When En was first used,

157
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
I was carrying this girl on my back.

158
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
If the King had noticed that,

159
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
I'm sure he would have come
straight to me.

160
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
But he didn't,
because she was wrapped in my hair.

161
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Hmm. I gotta admit, it sounds logical.

162
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
But I still don't quite see your point.

163
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
My point is that if she's covered,

164
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Wait a minute. You're saying
let Knuckle and Meleoron die

165
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
To accomplish that,

166
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Come on. Give me something.

167
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
The King will die soon.

168
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
He doesn't have very much time left.

169
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[gasps]

170
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
In just a few hours,

171
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
There. That should do it.

172
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
[gasps]

173
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
No!

174
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
We are far worse!

175
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
[dramatic music playing]

176
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
[Shaiapouf] Pitou.

177
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Pitou.

178
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Where are you?

179
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
Pitou!

180
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,000
[groans]

181
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[upbeat music playing]

182
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
[Gon] Next time, "The Word Is You."

183
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
And it isn't Killua.

184
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
[Shaiapouf] Nothing less, nothing more.

185
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
